== en60 lang=en
Today was one of the longest days I have had in a while. I woke up early because I had to finish the slides for my presentation, and then the train was late, so I ran the last few blocks to the office. My manager liked the slides, which was a relief, but then she asked me to lead the client call next week, and I am honestly nervous about it. At lunch I sat with two people from the design team and we talked about hiking trails near the lake. After work I called my mom, and she told me my grandmother is feeling better, which made me really happy. Now I am home, the tea is warm, and I just want to rest for a bit before I start thinking about tomorrow. I keep wondering whether I am ready for that call, and whether I should practice with a friend first. My friend Sam said he would help me on Sunday, so maybe we can meet at the coffee shop near the station and go through it twice. I think that would make me feel a lot calmer.
